\lambda a+\\mu b=2a+2b.$ \n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1754eccd-ec7f-5204-806f-ed41f26894fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327138} {:answer/id #uuid "58b7e4a1-6805-552d-86f2-f1434646a625" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =3.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327711} {:answer/id #uuid "63ebdee6-5ead-50c1-9a1a-f01abc2adffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327802} {:answer/id #uuid "a67826f4-23a8-5cfb-a73c-187b9a6eec4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328374} {:answer/id #uuid "f607dfd9-32a2-5e67-932b-093b37e029ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-2.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a67826f4-23a8-5cfb-a73c-187b9a6eec4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328374} :answer-field/id #uuid "703a83ec-ece6-50c6-955a-a6ccb5003bf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329373}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6df187f-d344-54eb-95de-18be02ffa7f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-42670" :question/problem "![](images/01/01940c9fa894d635300a49867da35d483b873a45d2a75204c20c58e4cb84c883.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/a0/a0d9fa1c366945e5e789b6361f929357af163db2e9be4a3ccc9023c12486aca6.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=2|r|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ has the opposite direction to $r$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=-2r.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=2|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-2s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =-2r-2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=-2r-2s.$ \n\nSince $s∦r,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dcfec14-cb0a-5093-aca2-c64dcab4c730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253787} {:answer/id #uuid "1272e74e-fb78-59d2-9d84-d72aa670ad11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253830} {:answer/id #uuid "3e10a9f2-1e2c-5cf1-b294-748c37da198c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254206} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9b310f-087d-588a-be38-6cb7b7a187b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255489} {:answer/id #uuid "cebf7021-3b8a-5c16-b5a9-e42a4a2ed96f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1272e74e-fb78-59d2-9d84-d72aa670ad11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253830} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d68256d-13fe-57b1-b3cf-f8ae54b5b98f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255937}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf2e5cbf-66fb-56e7-95be-719efd096999" :question/math-academy-id "q-120268" :question/problem "![](images/25/25717d521feeec25f7b4b722ca7b8a4ee9b5fdc8423bac06953e5f2adc8eef3d.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d5/d585c949d7de8cc3fa2d62bfb60990af12242c32ef3390e563f7e627844c5a88.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=3|r|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ and $r$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=3r.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=2|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-2s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =3r-2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=3r-2s.$ \n\nSince $s∦r,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0956f584-e832-537c-9bfd-df2ed29f604c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253740} {:answer/id #uuid "8e097b9e-5e91-54a9-9371-58923e289845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254922} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ddd4ba-6c17-5bcf-8e2d-4f52eaf316fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255291} {:answer/id #uuid "cc1c43e3-09e0-524d-a0a4-f5fb8a9c819c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255483} {:answer/id #uuid "e2fc6d53-d302-54b7-88b6-3eff72e7c370" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ and $\\mu =-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6ddd4ba-6c