lambda =2$ and $\\mu =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed1ac42e-951d-5ef5-af7a-bd888f1535e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344322} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a3fc608-70a9-52f3-b660-88c24389d51a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344538}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98730953-beae-5f36-b02e-39e84ea26f4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-77515" :question/problem "![](images/c8/c800644be3cc0ad0688d52948a4a2cb813cbe14b1fe899abe5a1d92613a687bf.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $r=\\lambda p+\\mu q$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/90/90272fad8af526de6e169faba8daae29210c1f502c4959d0e1829e5ad65476f0.png)\n\nIn $△OPR$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OP=2|p|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OP}$ and $p$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OP}=2p.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $PR=4|q|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ and $q$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=4q.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =2p+4q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $r=\\lambda p+\\mu q=2p+4q.$\n\nSince $p∦q,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =4$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c28aff5d-53e7-5f16-983d-538f4ce98117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c28aff5d-53e7-5f16-983d-538f4ce98117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365576} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cfd16dc-f42e-5638-89f3-68f27f774336" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81e0b22a-548d-5d2e-b32f-16412fc6cadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81e0b22a-548d-5d2e-b32f-16412fc6cadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365578} :answer-field/id #uuid "71b77659-ec75-56f7-ab9f-4c3596d182b4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365577}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "681d8619-9082-56b4-9422-241cad7644a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-326016" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f9ee37fe5f1cf32ba470b24e5d27b4164bd00a0caeae0536ae48d4cc5836c6d.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $t=\\lambda a+\\mu b$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/c9/c95e718a0c30e2be1f3678123eea0006b17fd781305c06a4f277488c2389337f.png)\n\nIn $△OXT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OX=\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot |a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OX}$ has the opposite direction to $a$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OX}=-\\frac{7}{4}a.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $XT=2|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{XT}$ has the opposite direction to $b$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-2b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\nt=\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-\\frac{7}{4}a-2b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda a+\\mu b=-\\frac{7}{4}a-2b.$\n\nSince $b∦a,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{7}{4}$ and $\\mu =-2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a9d3aac-2ddf-558e-9987-0dee3c2852ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2.5$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403880} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c5e6ea-81c8-564a-84fa-99f998a1a61d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2.5$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403881} {:answer/id #uuid "ed44e8da-0848-535d-a8ae-87bdbaa1daf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2.5$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403882} {:answer/id #uuid "8353c3d6-6092-5f38-bfd8-8a8168b1859c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403883} {:answer/id #uuid "aa67f058-afcd-51ee-97d4-c377ce896d7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2.5$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0c5e6ea-81c8-564a-84fa-99f998a1a61d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2.5$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403881} :answer-field/id #uuid "6554496f-6084-5a58-8758-7a159d646048" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403879}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8cb8830-d33b-5725-abf1-a6d3f309ef27" :question/math-academy-id "q-77452" :question/problem "![](images/16/1649e6c4ef2874cda2a7d7428b54220ef2a1790ba4b197c755165c48add0c31e.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+\\mu b$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7c/7cf17440c27765efb34b6a01c12a76ad4e980fc540307e2218227153661db5dd.png)\n\nIn $△OAC$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OA=2.5|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OA}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=2.5a.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $AC=3|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=3b.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =2.5a+3b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+\\mu b=2.5a+3b.$ \n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n$\\,$ $\\lambda =2.5$ and $\\mu =3$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420467 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f1fbbe3-94d8-5bd3-8727-4e6f9a832097" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420448} {:answer/id #uuid "90599886-7bfb-5b72-84ac-b60df87c5d99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420452} {:answer/id #uuid "a6826047-3513-5e97-9ed8-1ae795633fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420453} {:answer/id #uuid "b05969db-3a13-5b96-96be-8b739e33d310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420455} {:answer/id #uuid "cf620219-7b28-5e23-a450-b4abd046ba47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6826047-3513-5e97-9ed8-1ae795633fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420453} :answer-field/id #uuid "979e9c27-4560-5e47-8337-19ce5dc8192c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420463}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5f98ecb-0f26-50ae-9a82-cc334fd82c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-20413" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4bb7598c9ebae28be572508974cd025caa8f4a6c3313f025ff0f5ca55296334e.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $h=\\lambda f+\\mu g$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/43/43642acdb991827b4e1e16744e8a69507a383a1319ae07efde78480af4bab166.png)\n\nIn $△OFH$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OF=2|g|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OF}$ and $g$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=2g.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $FH=3|f|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FH}$ has the opposite direction to $f$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{FH}=-3f.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FH} \\\\  & =2g-3f \\\\  & =-3f+2g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $h=\\lambda f+\\mu g=-3f+2g.$\n\nSince $f∦g,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\mu =2$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514754 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd94222-3648-5492-8241-4b010da5c333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bd94222-3648-5492-8241-4b010da5c333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514759} :answer-field/id #uuid "01a589e1-3968-5f24-a7a9-df5b3459d167" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce52fb0c-e791-5450-871b-0e9a36cae631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce52fb0c-e791-5450-871b-0e9a36cae631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514784} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fd84807-e874-5f2c-879f-a22668b2264d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514760}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1d7e3219-6ed4-5e79-b442-f16e9eeecf24" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b6e5e69988b962627f39af49e25a904769a7de6bbebf8193e19d1540895ef992.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $r=\\lambda p+\\mu q$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](images/6b/6be1c7aa854a75ea143bc6b0b70317128d3f83f7868db4eb1ad50b326d223b8c.png)\n\nIn $△OMR$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OM=\\frac{1}{4}|q|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OM}$ and $q$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=\\frac{1}{4}q.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $MR=\\frac{4}{3}|p|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{MR}$ has the opposite direction to $p$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{MR}=-\\frac{4}{3}p.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MR} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}q-\\frac{4}{3}p \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}p+\\frac{1}{4}q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $$\n\\displaystyle r=\\lambda p+\\mu q=-\\frac{4}{3}p+\\frac{1}{4}q.\n$$\n\nSince $p∦q,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{4}{3}$ and $\\mu =\\frac{1}{4}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e30b8b0a-5c41-508a-800a-779854ec5eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e30b8b0a-5c41-508a-800a-779854ec5eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514787} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8b81958-e219-58a0-af4f-f9c9461153fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514777} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e5d37a4-d6f5-5dd8-8b8a-eac05883aa8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e5d37a4-d6f5-5dd8-8b8a-eac05883aa8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514763} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9f5d3fb-f5c7-582c-bbb3-23bc6fe37925" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-f