 and $\\mu=\\frac{3}{2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735258 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8e7cbc6-3c65-594c-8f00-2776cc76ee94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8e7cbc6-3c65-594c-8f00-2776cc76ee94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735261} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bddc27e-c0b1-5b16-ab38-836a4a97464d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "323a4f18-57fa-5e43-a681-52cbc1ad5403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "323a4f18-57fa-5e43-a681-52cbc1ad5403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735245} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e5e3f91-05d6-5c96-a4fa-368806a9ce8b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735255}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc8e6b34-f02b-5448-931c-94334c21f73e" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/9a/9adcf4f0295b807efed07a34d2bff2eee01a5229fd367f026fed6de705c34199.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/2c/2cf0ee7b5174b6d89944b5e3d6a48086048362ad029235a7ded707f735f4b722.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $10$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $4$ squares up. Thus $OX=\\frac{5}{2}|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=-\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $1$ square right and $1$ square down. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square up. Thus $XC=1|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-\\mathbf{b}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=-\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\mu=-1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186735262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8521e6a9-96fb-5355-bf53-2312c787ab2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8521e6a9-96fb-5355-bf53-2312c787ab2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735254} :answer-field/id #uuid "197a1d8b-a301-58c8-acff-0cf49ece00b7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07c71780-2ebd-5a1a-8b42-ea36774e7de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07c71780-2ebd-5a1a-8b42-ea36774e7de4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735241} :answer-field/id #uuid "5805f0a6-69aa-57bf-8d79-b19cc88666c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186735247}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb17691f-ad45-50d8-9bf1-066fefc0ee32" :question/problem "The vectors are drawn on a square grid, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\overrightarrow{OC}$.\n\n![Vector diagram](images/43/43d8df5853adab4bc9f7ae8138675c855dec0281cb0cd9b053539a116f8b20d5.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mu\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\mu=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "![Completed vector route](images/5a/5a64645ccdb41247aafd9b4ffb99718662e93aae73ae498428e2ceadda8e2c54.png)\n\nConstruct the route $O\\to X\\to C$, first parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nAlong $OX$, move $5$ squares right and $10$ squares up. A copy of $\\mathbf{b}$ moves $2$ squares right and $4$ squares up. Thus $OX=\\frac{5}{2}|\\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{OX}=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}$.\n\nAlong $XC$, move $6$ squares down. A copy of $\\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares up. Thus $XC=3|\\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\\overrightarrow{XC}=-3\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OX}+\\overrightarrow{XC}\\\\&=\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}-3\\mathbf{a}\\\\&=-3\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReorder the terms to match their vector names. Since $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, their coefficients are unique. Matching coefficients gives $\\lambda=-3$ and $\\mu=\\frac{5}{2}$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Two Scalar Factors in a Linear Combination"}]}
